---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/apps/rejoiner';
const title = "Rejoiner for Shopify: platform, creative work and service ownership";
const desc = "Evaluate lifecycle software alongside optional strategy and creative services, with a concrete brief, approval process and handover plan.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is Rejoiner only a managed service?",
    "answer": "No. Its current offer separates the software platform from optional Strategy Partner and Creative Partner services."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Rejoiner support SMS?",
    "answer": "Rejoiner documents SMS/MMS journeys. Confirm usage charges and which SMS responsibilities are included in your service scope."
  },
  {
    "question": "Will commissioned creatives automatically become portable assets?",
    "answer": "Agree reuse rights, export formats and third-party licences explicitly in the applicable agreement and handover plan."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/apps">App directory</a>
    <p class="badge mt-6">Operating review · November 25, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p>
  </section>
  <article class="container prose-shopify pb-16">
    <h2>Where Rejoiner can help</h2>
    <p>Rejoiner offers lifecycle software and optional professional services. Its <a class="link" href="https://www.rejoiner.com/pricing">platform and service breakdown</a> separates Strategy Partner guidance from Creative Partner production. This suits a merchant seeking either in-house operation with expert input or a partner to produce email work. Choose based on the work your team needs delivered, rather than a store-revenue threshold.</p>
    <h2>Software and services are separate decisions</h2>
    <p>The platform supports email journeys, segmentation and Shopify integration. The pricing page lists SMS usage separately; the <a class="link" href="https://www.rejoiner.com/products/text-messaging">text messaging page</a> describes SMS/MMS journeys. Establish which channels the service team will actually operate. Buying email creative services does not itself define a managed SMS brief.</p>
    <h2>Specify the service deliverables</h2>
    <p>Propose a service schedule listing each campaign, journey revision, copy draft, design, implementation and report. Strategy advice and finished production are different deliverables. Assign the merchant owner for product facts, offer validity and inventory, and the partner owner for production status. Record revision allowances and dependencies so a late product asset has a known consequence.</p>
    <h2>Proposed creative acceptance exercise</h2>
    <p>Give the team one real product brief with approved claims, image rights, a destination URL and eligibility rules. Request a draft, revision and rendered preview, then inspect the actual links, mobile layout, fallback content and audience definition. Record acceptance criteria before work begins. This is a proposed procurement exercise, not a test we performed or evidence of conversion lift.</p>
    <h2>Approval needs an explicit release step</h2>
    <p>The <a class="link" href="https://www.rejoiner.com/terms">published terms</a> tie services to a Service Order and treat delivered creatives as accepted. Agree how review deadlines, corrections and send authorization work in your order, including any expressly negotiated changes. An internal approval workflow should name who can release a campaign and who can pause it when an offer changes.</p>
    <h2>Proposed journey and channel exercise</h2>
    <p>Ask for a controlled demonstration of cart entry, purchase before the scheduled reminder, and a subsequent marketing opt-out. Inspect eligibility and queued actions for each channel in scope. Reconcile the Shopify order identity with the journey record. If an existing sender remains active, assign each flow to one sending system during the changeover and inspect old queues before enabling replacements.</p>
    <h2>Agree what can leave at handover</h2>
    <p>The published terms distinguish merchant data from Rejoiner materials and license access to the platform. Request explicit rights and formats for reusable templates, source artwork, copy, reports and customer exports before commissioning work. Identify third-party assets and licence restrictions. A handover should include journey logic, audience definitions, unresolved work and account access ownership; do not assume every creative asset transfers automatically.</p>
    <h2>Price the work as well as the software</h2>
    <p>Use the current quote for active-contact platform charges, professional services and channel usage. Add merchant review time, initial implementation and any overlap with the old provider. Estimate total program cost per eligible customer over the evaluation period; do not divide a monthly retainer by one campaign and call that its marginal send cost. Compare delivered work and released internal capacity alongside contribution.</p>
    <h2>Measure a service hypothesis</h2>
    <p>Before rollout, define whether the purchase is intended to improve production capacity, release consistency or incremental margin. Track approved work delivered and merchant hours required. For a controlled audience comparison, use net sales after discounts and refunds, subtract variable order costs and program costs once, and report the assigned audience denominator. Attributed revenue alone cannot establish the service caused an increase.</p>
    <h2>A practical selection rule</h2>
    <p>Choose the platform when your team can operate the channel; add guidance or production when those specific responsibilities need an owner. Resolve scope, approvals and reuse rights before signing. Use the <a class="link" href="/guides/email-sms-coordination">channel coordination guide</a> when separate sending systems remain, and the <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing">pricing worksheet</a> for the full program budget.</p>
    <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
